id: pm-vcs-j7mz
title: Define explicit retirement of native forge proposal and review history roots
description: "Phase 5 roots every proposed series in refs/forge-archive and preserves review revisions and catalog transitions in native commit/oplog history. This correctly prevents GC from losing reviewable changes after lease release, but retained proposal/history growth has no explicit retirement policy. Define an authorized and auditable lifecycle without weakening ref/oplog reachability or treating ordinary GC as obliteration. Distinct from abandoned upload receipts in pm-vcs-uploadretention."
type: Chore
status: open
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-14T20:11:29.024Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-14T20:11:55.651Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Specify which archive refs, review history and oplog transitions may be retired, who may authorize it, and what remains readable; prove GC never drops still-referenced proposals or review outcomes; preserve typed authorized obliteration as a separate operation."
